WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
- One of your friends and co-stars,

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.153
on "The Flight Attendant"...

00:00:03.153 --> 00:00:04.230
I love "The Flight Attendant".

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.063
I'm so excited about the second season.

00:00:05.063 --> 00:00:06.910
- Thank you, thank you! (applause)

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:07.770
- So excited.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.150
She really helped you
through everything, right?

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:09.983
- Yeah.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.250
Zosia, yes.
- Yeah.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.083
- Thank you.

00:00:13.083 --> 00:00:15.350
Zosia is my co-star and my best friend.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.690
She helped me so much through season two.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.880
She basically lived with me the
last few months of shooting.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.293
We just moved in together.

00:00:24.552 --> 00:00:26.270
I don't think I would have

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:28.072
gotten to work some days without her.

00:00:28.072 --> 00:00:28.905
(chuckles)

00:00:28.905 --> 00:00:30.447
- Oh, I have those friends.

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:31.280
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:32.590
And I never thought I had to

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.470
depend on anyone like that before.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.120
I really depended on her,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.092
and she helped me through so much.

00:00:38.092 --> 00:00:39.650
She would have days off,

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.508
and she would, oh, I'm gonna cry.

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:44.380
She would come to work on days
she didn't have to be there.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:45.750
And come and have lunch with me.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.180
And I'm like, "You have
your day off today."

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.110
She's like, "I'm coming in."

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.640
'Cause she heard I was
having a rough time,

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.681
and she would sit in my trailer.

00:00:53.681 --> 00:00:55.250
She's the best.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.760
I'm very lucky that I had her.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.670
- Female friendships,
as far as I'm concerned

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:02.740
are my most healthy
relationships I feel like,

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:03.670
other than my family.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:07.530
And they're so good for us
because I feel like we connect.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.210
Even when I was married,

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.350
you connect in a different way

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.649
than you do with like your girlfriend.

00:01:11.649 --> 00:01:12.482
- Totally different way.

00:01:12.482 --> 00:01:13.315
- Yeah.
- It's totally different.

00:01:13.315 --> 00:01:14.148
There's nothing like it.

00:01:14.148 --> 00:01:14.981
- It's so good for us.

00:01:14.981 --> 00:01:17.040
- I'm always promoting
that with my everyone.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.070
I'm like, "You need to have
good girlfriends in your life."

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:20.580
It's so, so, so important.
- Yeah, you know what?

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.170
I don't even know if I trust a girl

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.300
that doesn't have a girlfriend.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.590
- That's a little strange.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:26.070
You gotta have a good girlfriend.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.270
It says a lot about you.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:28.507
- I know, someone was once told me,

00:01:28.507 --> 00:01:29.350
"I don't really have girlfriends"

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:30.730
and I was like, "That's not shocking."

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:31.843
- Yeah, no, it's weird.

00:01:32.739 --> 00:01:34.020
- I was like, "It's not shocking news."

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.660
- It's very clear (laughing).

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.840
- And we call each other out,
but we lift each other up.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:39.580
It's like a really healthy... anyway.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:40.633
- I totally agree.

